From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 23:35:58 +0800
Subject: dt-bindings: net: qca808x: document qca,led-mode

Add a qca,led-mode DT property for QCA8081 PHYs to select one of
the datasheet-defined LED preset modes.

The property programs the MMD7 LED control registers for the three
PHY LED outputs during PHY initialization and accepts values 1..3.

Update the binding example to show a PHY using LED mode 2.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
(cherry picked from commit 02ff2813f642ddb6053441075ce3257c960ae6e2)
[SuperKali: ported from radxa/kernel linux-7.0.11]
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/qca,qca808x.yaml | 12 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/qca,qca808x.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/qca,qca808x.yaml
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/qca,qca808x.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/qca,qca808x.yaml
@@ -39,6 +39,17 @@ properties:
   vdd125-supply:
     description: (1.25v to 1.98v) LDO regulator power supply.
 
+  qca,led-mode:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    description: |
+      Select one of the vendor-defined LED preset modes described in the
+      datasheet. The selected mode programs the MMD7 LED control registers for
+      all three PHY LED outputs during PHY initialization.
+    enum:
+      - 1
+      - 2
+      - 3
+
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
@@ -52,6 +63,7 @@ examples:
         ethernet-phy@0 {
             compatible = "ethernet-phy-id004d.d101";
             reg = <0>;
+            qca,led-mode = <2>;
 
             vdd18-supply = <&phy_vreg_1v8>;
 
-- 
Armbian

